# Target C-II - refined flat-pentagon hidden-derivative rank

**Date:** 2026-09-14
**Base theorem:** `target_c_flat_pentagon_hidden_derivative_rank_2026-09-14.md`
**Dependencies:** certified minimax gap `g=0.002123`; low-t pentagon sea
**Claim class:** proof-only rank refinement; theorem-state authority unchanged

## LEVEL I STATUS

`STILL OPEN`

The base hidden-derivative theorem proves, for a sufficiently flat selected pentagon
family `P` of size `p`,

\[
\operatorname{rank}(H_P|_{\ker C_{face}})
\ge {7p\over3}-2f+\sigma_C,
\tag{RR.1}
\]

where `f` is the number of bounded exceptional faces and `sigma_C>=0` is the closure
corank.  Its numerical insertion paid `2f` by the coarse inequality `f<=Q`.  On the
same `R_F=o(D)` branch there is a sharper payment.

Let `p_5` be the total pentagon count and `X=Q-f`.  Fix the sufficiently small
flatness neighborhood needed for the nonzero local minor in the base theorem.  Residual
conservation deletes only `o(D)` pentagons, so

\[
p_5-p=o(D).
\]

Every nonpentagonal exceptional face contributes at least one unit to

\[
X=\sum_{d\ge6}(d-5)n_d,
\]

hence `N_{>=6}<=X`.  Therefore

\[
\boxed{f-p=N_{\ge6}+(p_5-p)\le X+o(D).}
\tag{RR.2}
\]

Substituting (RR.2) in (RR.1) gives the stronger source-level rank bound

\[
\boxed{
\operatorname{rank}(H_P|_{\ker C_{face}})
\ge {p\over3}-2X+\sigma_C-o(D).
}
\tag{RR.3}
\]

Now put `s=sqrt(Delta_2)`, `g=0.002123`, and `C_0=2s+g`.  The certified low-`t`
ledgers give

\[
{p\over D}\ge
\pi+C_0-{5t\over2}+\delta+{\kappa\over2}-o(1),
\]

and

\[
{X\over D}\le
{9t\over4}-\pi-{C_0\over2}-\delta-{\kappa\over4}+o(1).
\]

Thus

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {1\over D}\operatorname{rank}(H_P|_{\ker C_{face}})
\ge
{7\pi\over3}+{4C_0\over3}-{16t\over3}
+{7\delta\over3}+{2\kappa\over3}.
}
\tag{RR.4}
\]

At the certified Section-171 endpoint

\[
t_{23}={4\over9}(\pi+s)+0.0017327,
\]

dropping the nonnegative bonuses yields

\[
\boxed{
\liminf {1\over D}\operatorname{rank}(H_P|_{\ker C_{face}})
\ge0.159401074123032\ldots .
}
\tag{RR.5}
\]

The earlier `f<=Q` payment, updated to the same `g,t_{23}`, gives only
`0.153726924123032...`; (RR.2) gains exactly `2X=0.00567415` at the endpoint.

The scalar part of (RR.4) stays positive until

\[
\boxed{
t<{7\pi+4C_0\over16}
=1.851133939377513\ldots .}
\tag{RR.6}
\]

This rank counts independent first-order radial coordinates of actual inactive hidden
leaf chords after every ordinary bounded-face contact-closure equation is imposed.  It
does not provide a common shortening sign or diameter-feasible flex.  C-II remains
open.
